# Check every text file out with LF, whatever a machine's `core.autocrlf` is set to. A Windows clone
# that gets CRLF rewrites the exact bytes some checks compare: Biome reports the whole file as
# reformatted, the skill's stamp stops matching, and a spec's byte limit counts the extra CRs, so
# `npm run lint` and part of `npm test` fail on the checkout rather than on the change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Media is never line-ending-normalized (`text=auto` detects these anyway; naming them keeps a
# future reader from having to trust the heuristic).
*.gif binary
*.png binary
*.mp4 binary
